                <pb facs="0141" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg23"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2—Memorandum]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rights and Immunities at Sea During
                    War</hi></head>
                <p>As regards the second point, we recognize that some of the most troublesome
                    questions in our relations are those which have arisen out of rights and
                    immunities at sea during war. The controversies and <pb facs="0142" n="24"
                        xml:id="pg24"/> disputes engendered by this have in the past been pregnant
                    with the danger of aggravating and extending hostilities. Misunderstandings and
                    fears springing from this source have been a frequent, but we believe avoidable,
                    cause of friction between our two countries. We have resolved, therefore, that
                    in the light of the new situation created by the Pact of Paris, we shall examine
                    the question fully and frankly together on all its bearings.</p>
            </div>
